title: "MPI Krylov: Parallel Krylov Subspace Solvers with Communication-Avoiding Methods"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-24
url: "https://github.com/chenxinye/mpi_krylov"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenxinye/mpi_krylov"
keywords:
  - "Krylov methods"
  - "MPI"
  - "parallel computing"
  - "communication-avoiding algorithms"
  - "iterative solvers"
  - "sparse linear systems"
  - "preconditioners"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  MPI Krylov is a high-performance parallel library implementing
  Krylov subspace methods for solving large-scale sparse linear systems.
  It features communication-avoiding variants (CA-CG, CA-GMRES),
  pipelined methods, and various preconditioners (Jacobi, ILU(0),
  Additive Schwarz, Polynomial) optimized for distributed-memory systems.
  The library utilizes advanced MPI techniques including halo exchange
  and non-blocking communication for optimal scalability.
